364	     1	// The fixture helper's isolation from the HOST's git configuration.
365	     2	//
366	     3	// A scratch repo in a tmpdir exists for the length of one test, so a signature on
367	     4	// its commits buys nothing — and inheriting the ambient `commit.gpgsign` costs
368	     5	// twice. It is slow: every fixture commit becomes a round trip to a signing
369	     6	// service, measured at 202ms per makeRepo against 38ms without. And it is
370	     7	// fragile in the way that matters most: when the service degrades, each commit
371	     8	// blocks on it and the descriptors pile up behind it until git fails
372	     9	// process-wide, taking the suite with it for a reason that has nothing to do
373	    10	// with the code under test.
374	    11	//
375	    12	// This test pins the isolation rather than the speed, so it means the same thing
376	    13	// on a runner with no signing configured at all: it forces a hostile ambient
377	    14	// config — signing on, pointed at a program that always fails — and requires the
378	    15	// fixture to be built anyway. Without the helper's own override, git refuses the
379	    16	// commit and makeRepo throws.
380	    17	//
381	    18	// GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL is set BEFORE the dynamic import because the helper snapshots
382	    19	// process.env into its GIT_ENV at module load; a static import at the top of this
383	    20	// file would read the real environment and prove nothing.
